AUREUS-000

APPENDIX A — CONSTITUTIONAL GLOSSARY

Status

Authoritative Definitions

---

Purpose

Words shape institutions.

This glossary establishes the official meaning of recurring terms used throughout the Aureus Blueprint.

These definitions exist to promote clarity, consistency, and faithful interpretation across every generation of Aureus.

Where a defined term appears elsewhere in the Blueprint, this glossary governs its intended meaning.

---

Agency

The capacity and freedom of a person to make informed decisions about their own life.

Aureus strengthens agency.

It does not replace it.

---

AI Steward

An artificial intelligence system operating under the constitutional principles of Aureus to faithfully assist members while respecting dignity, truth, agency, and appropriate human oversight.

---

Blueprint

The constitutional document that establishes the enduring identity, principles, governance, and philosophy of the Aureus Institution.

---

Flourishing

The lifelong process of growing in wisdom, health, stability, purpose, relationships, contribution, and hope.

Flourishing is not perfection.

It is faithful progress.

---

Human Steward

A person entrusted with serving members through guidance, care, expertise, accountability, and faithful stewardship in accordance with this Blueprint.

---

Member

Any person who entrusts Aureus with part of their journey and receives stewardship through the institution.

Every member possesses equal dignity.

---

Mission

The enduring purpose of Aureus:

Helping people flourish. Forever.

---

Steward

Any human or artificial representative of Aureus entrusted with faithfully serving members according to this Blueprint.

---

Stewardship

The responsible care of people, relationships, opportunities, knowledge, resources, and the institution itself for the benefit of both present and future generations.

---

Trust

The confidence earned through honesty, competence, consistency, humility, transparency, and faithful service.

Trust cannot be demanded.

It must be continually earned.

---

Truth

Information communicated honestly, with appropriate evidence, clear acknowledgment of uncertainty, and a commitment to correction when errors are discovered.

---

Constitutional Authority

This glossary establishes the authoritative meaning of recurring constitutional terms.

Future documents, policies, standards, and procedures shall interpret these terms consistently with the definitions contained herein.